WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
[ Music ]

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:08.600
[Christmas Seals fight Tuberculosis]

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:14.780
[The National Tuberculosis Association in
cooperation with the United States]

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.160
[Office of Indian Affairs presents]

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:23.360
[Another to Conquer]

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.120
[The cast, Slow-Talker... Howard Gorman, Don
his grandson... Sammy Day, Nema, his granddaughter...

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.420
Geraldine H. Birdsbill, Robert a friend...
Richard Hogner, Director... W. W. Peter, M.D.]

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.930
[Director... Edgar G. Ulmer, Camera... Robert
Cline, Sound... Clarence Townsend, Consultant...

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.930
Ruth Underhill, Ph. D., Editor... H. E. Mandl;
RCA, Springer Pictures Inc.]

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.820
[The generous assistance of the Navajo Service
is gratefully acknowledged.]

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.960
[Narrator:] Long before the white man came
to the new world, the American Indians occupied

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.770
the broad land we now called the United States.

00:00:56.770 --> 00:01:03.770
They were a great people of many tribes. Some
lived in the desert, others on the plains,

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:08.740
still others in the forest, on the lakes and
rivers.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:14.810
Their natural enemies were numerous. And in
addition, tribal wars and feuds took their

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:21.270
toll. Yet always, the Indians faced their
foes without fear.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:32.280
Their sons and daughters of today face new
enemies. One of them is a cruel disease- tuberculosis,

00:01:32.549 --> 00:01:38.869
which steals away the strength of the victim
until he is lifeless.

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:45.869
Yet Indians of today have not lost the courage
of their fathers and this courage will not

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:51.950
fail them. This enemy too, they will conquer.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:02:01.290
[Sound of horse and wagon approaching.]

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:14.760
[Slow-Talker:] Never look back to the house
of the dead. It is our custom that we leave

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:30.330
our dead in peace. Grandson, your father has
gone back to earth. We start anew.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.880
[Don:] Grandpa, will the cough kill my mother
too?

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:44.800
[Slow-Talker:] O'la. Who knows.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:53.000
[Melancholy music]

00:02:53.180 --> 00:03:00.300
[A dozen years swept on. Zonchee, the mother,
died, too. But grandfather Slow-Talker held

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:07.400
the little family together: the lovely Nema
and Don his ardent admirer. 

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:13.520
Robert, their neighbor, was a frequent visitor. Together they worked and played and took part in the folk ways.]

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:41.160
[Chanting, singing, and drumming are heard and people are shown moving in a circle around a fire.]

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:56.260
An elder begins speaking.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:04:01.580
[Don:] Slow-Talker is running. We have always
gone out to meet our enemies, but now no more.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.549
Now we die.

00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:09.549
[Robert:] Yes, we die. But it is sad. First
your mother, then your father died of tuberculosis.

00:04:09.819 --> 00:04:14.080
[Don:] He says we die because we do not keep
the old customs.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:21.080
[Robert:] I wonder. Slow-Talker's brave, yes.
But he may be mistaken; the old weapons of

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:23.379
our fathers cannot fight tuberculosis.

00:04:23.379 --> 00:04:27.359
[Nema:] You mean, we should heed the white
doctors?

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:30.700
[Don:] I am loyal to the old man.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:43.340
[ Chanting ]

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:47.260
[Robert:] Nema, I have news. I am going to
the boarding school.

00:04:47.349 --> 00:04:50.869
[Nema:] Yeah, is your mind really made up?

00:04:50.869 --> 00:04:56.240
[Robert:] Yes, I honor our people, respect
them, but white people have much to share

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:59.319
with us. I will learn something and live better.

00:04:59.319 --> 00:05:06.319
[Nema:] And... you will come back.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:13.080
[Chanting and drumming.]

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:26.520
[Music plays as Robert saddles up his horse.]

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:33.740
[Robert:] Goodbye Nema

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:34.800
[Nema:] Goodbye Robert.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:39.800
[Robert:] Goodbye Slow-Talker.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:42.560
[Slow-Talker:] Goodbye.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:52.780
[Nema watches as the men and horses ride away ]

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:01.860
[Slow-Talker:] Forsaking the ways of his people.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:26.040
[Horses galloping down a hill and across a desert landscape.]

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:35.340
[The two men are shown walking towards a white building.]

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:41.020
[Narrator:] The ways part for these two comrades.
Good luck to you says Don, as Robert faces

00:06:41.199 --> 00:06:48.199
new experiences in school. It all seems strange
at first but Robert soon likes it. 

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:50.339
And he learns fast.

00:06:50.339 --> 00:06:56.629
He discovers the wisdom left by others in
books. Both mind and hand are trained. He

00:06:56.629 --> 00:07:00.770
learns the skillful use of tools and machines.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:06.209
Order and cleanliness become part of his daily
life.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:13.200
Sports and games help him to build a strong
body and fit muscles and train him in the

00:07:13.319 --> 00:07:17.719
art of team play with his fellows.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:19.940
[ Music ]

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:22.700
[Whistle blows]

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:29.900
[The boys gather around the coach.]

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:33.660
[Coach:] Boys, a doctor has come to make the
physical examination.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:41.760
[Doctor:] Boys, you all look strong, but there
are the invisible worms that can harm the

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:48.199
body. We call them germs, and so each student
gets a physical examination.

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:51.220
Robert, I think I'll start with you first.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.420
[The doctor is shown examining and listening to Robert's chest.]

00:07:54.500 --> 00:08:00.980
[Doctor:] Ever thump a covered water barrel to hear
how full it is? This is just like that. Doctors

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:05.340
learn how lungs sound when healthy and when
sick.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:17.020
[Robert:] Warriors put their ears to the ground
to hear the footsteps of their enemy.

00:08:17.249 --> 00:08:24.249
[Doctor:] Is that so? We have the same idea.
Lungs make sound, one kind of sound when healthy,

00:08:24.279 --> 00:08:29.239
another kind when sick. Stand here please,
Robert.

00:08:29.239 --> 00:08:35.659
Chin up there, shoulders against. That's it.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:43.220
X-rays we call them. The rays pass right through
the body and throw a shadow picture on the

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:44.940
film in the holder.

00:08:44.949 --> 00:08:50.729
Take a deep breath, hold it. Finished.

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:59.880
Now, tomorrow when this film is developed
I will show you a picture of your heart and lungs.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:09.300
Here, Robert, is the X-ray picture of your
lungs taken yesterday. These are the collarbones.

00:09:10.769 --> 00:09:22.049
The ribs, lung, all healthy, healthy, all
healthy but that spot, see it? That spot is

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:26.100
made by tuberculosis, Robert.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:36.180
[Robert:] No. Tuberculosis? But I am so well.
I don't cough, it can't be.

00:09:36.339 --> 00:09:43.329
[Doctor:] Don't be discouraged, Robert. The
lung will heal if you go at once to a sanatorium

00:09:43.329 --> 00:09:48.339
and stay there until the doctor says you may
go home.

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:55.019
[Narrator:] And so Robert finds himself in
the sanatorium, where under the guidance of

00:09:55.019 --> 00:10:01.079
doctors and nurses, he learns to fight his
enemy in bed.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:15.800
[A man on a horse comes galloping through a canyon.]

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:20.780
[He pulls up and dismounts.]

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.840
[Nema:] How is Robert? Is he all right?

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:30.200
[Don:] He looks healthy.

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:48.280
[Slow-Talker:] He's just lazy, easygoing,
in bed, bah. 

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:52.860
How long do you think he'll be in the hospital?

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:59.760
[Don:] I don't know. A long time, maybe. The
nurse says Robert must be quiet in bed [cough].

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:03.310
I told Robert he's a sissy.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:10.300
[Slow-Talker:] Our ancestors were brave. They
stood on their feet and fought their enemies

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:24.440
until they were whipped. What's this I hear
today? Young men lazing around in bed. Bah.

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:35.580
[Nema:] But grandfather, perhaps that is not
the way to fight this enemy, on their feet.

00:11:35.949 --> 00:11:38.969
When they do, they die.

00:11:38.969 --> 00:11:42.879
[ Don coughing ]

00:11:42.879 --> 00:11:45.459
[Nema:] Don, don't you think you should go
to the doctor?

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:50.120
[Don:] No, I am strong. Tomorrow I will be
better.

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:54.519
[Doctor:] Hello Robert. Mind if I sit down?

00:11:54.519 --> 00:11:59.350
[Doctor:] Now that you're almost well I'd
like to tell you more about this disease.

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:06.350
You can help your people better than I can
to understand.

00:12:06.879 --> 00:12:13.879
Here's the left lung. Here's the right. Here's
the windpipe.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:21.160
The lung is soft like a sponge and it works
like a bellows. Tuberculosis usually starts

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:24.319
up here.

00:12:24.319 --> 00:12:31.319
It may seem harmless at first, and heal in
a short time. But, sometimes it spreads.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:40.120
Like a little patch of weeds, bit by bit it
destroys the lung.

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:48.830
Then the man begins to cough and spit up damaged
lung flesh. It spreads more.

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:59.830
The man loses his taste for food. He loses
weight, he gets weak and maybe spits up blood.

00:13:01.069 --> 00:13:06.499
He goes weaker and thinner and at last he
dies.

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:11.480
[Robert:] Is there no medicine to stop this
disease?

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:18.720
[Doctor:] No. Though men have hunted for such
a medicine for years. But nature can stop

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:27.210
it, and heal it as it heals other sicknesses.
Robert, what do we do for a broken leg?

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:29.020
[Robert:] We tie it up with fixing straps.

00:13:29.029 --> 00:13:36.029
[Doctor:] Exactly. Why? To keep it quiet so
it can heal. Doctors call that a splint.

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:43.810
We cannot tie up the lung, but we can rest
it by lying quietly in bed and gaining strength

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:47.120
from good food.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:51.329
[Robert:] That makes sense. Now, will you
tell me again about that little operation

00:13:51.329 --> 00:13:55.110
you did on me so I will be able to explain
it to my people.

00:13:55.110 --> 00:14:04.430
[Doctor:] It is called pneumothorax. That
means air in the chest. Here, let me show you.

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:16.580
A small hollow needle is pushed through the
chest wall. Air flows in. The soft lung collapses

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:19.720
like squeezing wool.

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:28.840
It cannot breathe, it rests, it heals. When
it is all well again inside, the lung is allowed

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:33.900
to blow up and breathe again as before.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:40.399
[Robert:] Wonderful. But here's what puzzles
me. What causes the disease? You told me once

00:14:40.399 --> 00:14:46.240
before it was caused by a germ, but what is
a germ?

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:56.200
[Doctor:] Well, it's really a tiny living
thing. Some call it the invisible worm.

00:14:56.209 --> 00:15:04.229
But it is alive. It grows. I can prove it
to you. Come, to the laboratory.

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:24.380
[Doctor:] Here in this tube is a kind of jelly,
clean, nothing on it. 

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:29.080
Here is another, something growing on it.

00:15:29.089 --> 00:15:38.909
A short time ago it was as clean as this one.
Do you know what that is? Millions of tuberculosis germs.

00:15:39.089 --> 00:15:47.849
A tiny bit of spit from a sick man was smeared
on here and it was put away in a warm place.

00:15:47.949 --> 00:15:50.999
The germs grew like a field of corn.

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:57.439
[Robert:] Oh, so when a few germs on the lungs
of a sick person get into the lungs of another,

00:15:57.439 --> 00:15:58.519
they start growing?

00:15:58.519 --> 00:16:03.889
[Doctor:] That's exactly right and that is
why sick people should be in the sanatorium.

00:16:03.889 --> 00:16:09.559
There, they can't spread the seeds of their
disease to others.

00:16:09.559 --> 00:16:16.559
We fight a range fire by clearing a strip.
The fire can't jump.

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:23.920
[Narrator:] Now you see Robert, why your people
suffer so much from tuberculosis. They crowd

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:26.949
together, somewhat careless about spitting.

00:16:26.949 --> 00:16:32.559
When people are not clean, it becomes easy
for the germ to get from one to another. Some

00:16:32.559 --> 00:16:37.660
people don't eat right and they become weak
and cannot fight the germs.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.939
[Sound of sheep baaaa-ing]

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:47.579
[Narrator:] Sheep-dipping time. From all directions
for miles around, the sheep and goats are

00:16:47.579 --> 00:16:52.569
brought to be dipped in a harmless solution
under the direction of government experts.

00:16:52.569 --> 00:16:58.439
This ensures a fine, healthy crop of wool.
Everybody has a good time, everybody helps.

00:16:58.439 --> 00:17:05.080
But the heavy work is done by sturdy young
men like Don.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:35.040
[Sounds of sheep, gates opening and closing, splashing, people shouting to one another. Men are shown handling and dipping the animals.]

00:17:44.720 --> 00:18:04.720
[A man is shown crouching, covering his mouth. Then he is helped to a waiting car, and the driver starts the engine.]

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:13.700
[As the car drives away, men on horseback come into view on the same dirt road.]

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:19.000
[A doctor in a white coat emerges from a house; the screen door slams.]

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:27.060
[Doctor:] Slow-Talker, Don is very sick. He
has tuberculosis. 

00:18:27.060 --> 00:18:32.540
The heavy work at the sheep dip started his lung to bleed.

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:40.480
[Robert:] The doctor said I was a good fighter.
I did what he said. Poor Don.

00:18:40.539 --> 00:18:46.980
He did not understand. Nema, don't you think
the doctor should examine you too?

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:51.090
[Nema:] Oh, Robert, do you think I could have
it?

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:55.840
[Robert:] Anyone can have it. It is passed
from one to another.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:02.840
[Slow-Talker:] I take Nema.

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:14.020
And a doctor shall examine me too.

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:22.780
[Doctor:] So you see, Nema's lungs are all
right. Now we look at your chest.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:31.280
Here is the shadow of tuberculosis in your
lung. You have had it a long time, but it has

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:38.080
not killed you. You are a strong man, stronger
than the disease.

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:45.080
[Slow-Talker:] Then it is true that I have
given the disease to my family.

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:49.100
[The doctor nods solemnly.]

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:56.110
[Don:] Grandpa, will the cough kill my mother
too?

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:59.680
[Doctor:] Slow-Talker Don is very sick.

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:08.260
[Slow-Talker:] Now, I know the enemy. I too
will fight him with knowledge, your way.

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:23.720
Go my children. I stay. May you have many
children, healthy and strong.

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:33.220
[ Music ]

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:49.200
[A woman walks toward a small native dwelling and enters. A baby is in its mother's arms.]

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:54.500
[Woman:] What a fine baby you have. Grandfather
will be so proud.

00:20:54.640 --> 00:21:00.200
[The mother is shown visiting Slow-Talker at the sanitorium and showing him the baby.]

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:07.200
[ Music ]

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:15.820
[Narrator:] Slow-Talker, we salute you. The
enemy has taken away your beloved Don and

00:21:15.820 --> 00:21:18.660
Don's parents.

00:21:18.669 --> 00:21:25.299
Now you yearn to go home, to mingle with the
people, the fields and hills and waters all

00:21:25.299 --> 00:21:27.360
these you love.

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:34.360
Yet, you choose to stay. You will not bring
the enemy to their fireside. By your example,

00:21:34.420 --> 00:21:40.100
the people again will conquer.

00:21:40.100 --> 00:21:55.460
[ Music swells, and the couple with the baby are shown walking, then pausing and smiling at one another.]

00:21:55.500 --> 00:22:03.700
[The End]

